Subject: [PATCH 1/2] =?UTF-8?q?simplify:=20fold=20neg(neg(x))=20to=20x=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20the=20bitwise=20double-negation=20identity?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Neg is the sign-bit XOR for floats and its own inverse in the
two's-complement ring for integers, so the double flip is exact in
both domains: NaN payloads, NaN signs and ±0 survive bit-for-bit,
INT_MIN included. The fold lives in try_simplify_with_types's new
UnaryOp arm, keyed off the existing NegDef map (types line up by
construction — the same SSA-typing invariant the x - (neg y) fold
already relies on), with its own CCC_SIMPLIFY_SKIP family 'negneg'
for bisection. Chains collapse in one sweep (neg^3 -> neg + copies,
neg^4 -> x + copies) because the prebuilt def map links every Neg to
its original source. No use-count guard: the rewrite is pure work
deletion.

The composition with the FMA neg-peel closes the shipped defect's
shape to GCC parity: t = -x; u = -t; r = fma(t, b, c); return r + u
now compiles to ONE vfnmadd + vadd (was 2 vxorpd + vfmadd + vadd;
GCC's exact family selection and operand form). The outer reader no
longer reads the inner link at all, so the peel's deletion is sound
by the closure rule; chains that DO reach the peel with a surviving
outer reader keep both links (unit test pinned, unchanged).

Gate pins updated to the strictly-stronger truths: chain_live now
demands ZERO sign masks + one negated family (was 2 masks/0
families); chain_pin's site reads the OUTER link which the fold
rewrites to x, so the fma takes the PLAIN family (was vfnmadd
reading the materialised inner). GCC oracles recorded in the gate
comments; the float add-of-neg -> sub fold (GCC drops chain_pin's
last mask with it) is documented as the designed follow-up — it
needs its own NaN-sign-latitude analysis.

Tests: 7 new simplify units (int/f32/f64 folds, chain-link
mechanics, non-neg source, constant, non-Neg unary negative
controls). Validation: cargo 3099/0; ISA gate PASS with the new
pins; cross-PR battery bit-exact (4 cfgs x 2 batteries); corpus
728/0/20 AB-diff 0 with CCC_VERIFY_IR=abort armed; correctness
oracle 57/57; 52 contract gates PASS; fmt + clippy clean.
