Subject: [PATCH 2/2] x86-64 ISA: -mfma implies the VEX chain, GCC-exact
 (fma-implies-vex)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FMA3 exists only in the VEX encoding — there is no legacy-SSE FMA —
so an explicit -mfma implies -mavx and its full prerequisite chain.
Oracle (gcc 14.2 -Q --help=target): -march=x86-64 -mfma reports
avx, sse4.1, sse4.2 all ENABLED with avx2 still disabled; -mavx alone
leaves fma disabled — the implication is one-directional. The pre-fix
ceiling declined the families at every march level without built-in
AVX, so fma(-a,b,-c) at -march=x86-64-v2 -mfma compiled to xorpd + a
libm call where GCC emits one vfnmsub132sd; the plain SSE2 baseline +
-mfma declined the same way (GCC enables there too — the march
ceiling is not a hard ceiling for explicit -m feature flags).

The -mfma CLI arm now mirrors the -mavx arm (clear the prerequisite
denials, enable avx + the sse4.2/4.1/ssse3/sse3 chain), keeping
later-flag-wins in both directions: a later -mno-avx / -mno-sse4.1 /
-mno-sse still kills the chain (their arms set the denial flags the
ceiling consults; -mno-sse's arm already carries the sticky-disable
semantics for march profiles), and -mfma after -mno-sse re-enables
the vector file (gcc: -mno-sse -mfma -> sse enabled; the reverse
order errors on FP-returning TUs in both compilers).

End-to-end matrix (lccc vs gcc, d1 chain shape): v2+mfma 1/1,
x86-64+mfma 1/1, v2+mfma+mno-avx 0/0, x86-64+mfma+mno-sse4.1 0/0,
v2 alone 0/0, mfma-before-march 1/1, mno-sse-then-mfma 1/1,
mfma-then-mno-sse error/error. The decline keeps __builtin_fma's
single-rounding contract via the libm fallback — exactly 8 fma@PLT
on the gate corpus, byte-count-identical to GCC's decline (never a
silent mul+add double rounding).

Tests: 7 new cli units asserted on x86_isa() itself (the final ISA
the pipeline consults), covering both orders of every conflict.
Gate: new 4c section (10 pins across the 4 target classes — families
inline, negated families inline, no ymm, shared-negation mask-free,
denial matrix with the libm-fallback count). Validation: cargo
3106/0; ISA gate PASS; cross-PR battery bit-exact; corpus 728/0/20
AB-diff 0 with CCC_VERIFY_IR=abort armed; 53 contract gates PASS;
fmt + clippy clean.
